; Command file for the main menu, 15 entries

; Line with a semicolon as the first character are comment lines and are
; ignored, as are blank lines containing nothing.

; The first line is the title for the menu

Main Menu

; Now come the menu entries, use the key provided to help you.  Command key
; goes in the first columnm followed by the name of the command, the
; minimum access level required to access the command, and lastly, the
; flags necessary to access the command (and X means that flag is on, -
; means it is off)

; ********************** *** ********
G Good-Bye (Log off)       0 --------
H Help With Commands       5 --------
Y Yell at SysOp            0 --------
C Change Setup             5 --------
F File Areas               5 --------
T Time Remaining           0 --------
B Bulletins                0 --------
J Join TransAmiga          0 --------
M Message Areas            5 --------
P Post Message to Node     5 --------
U User List                5 --------
L Leave Feedback           0 --------
O Online Games             5 --------
V Version Info             0 --------
W Who's Online?            0 --------
